# Own-wording spells of Grim Hollow Player's Guide (2024), chunk 2 (names 52 to 101 in alphabetical order). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Illusory Instrument": ["Conjure a weightless illusory copy of an instrument for 10 minutes. A Bonus Action triggers sound effects, a beat, or recordings.",
 "Touch a mundane musical instrument you know and conjure an illusory copy shaped by your fondest memory of it. The copy acts like the real thing but weighs nothing and only you can touch it. It works as a Spellcasting Focus. It vanishes if you move 10 ft away from it, or when you end the spell (no action). As a Bonus Action you can have it do one of these. **Mimic.** Imitate a basic everyday sound such as a bird, footsteps or a slamming door. **Beat.** Play a simple beat at the tempo you choose. **Loop.** Record whatever is played on it and replay it on a loop. **Record.** Record and replay any noise it can pick up within 15 ft, such as conversation or a royal decree."],
"Incite Riot": ["Wisdom save or creatures within 30 ft are Charmed and attack the nearest foe. Repeat the save each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Wave the red handkerchief and choose any number of creatures within 30 ft that can see you. Each makes a Wisdom save, with Advantage if you or your allies are fighting it. On a fail it is Charmed until the spell ends or until you or your allies damage it. A Charmed creature is Friendly to you and your allies. On its turn it must use its action to make melee attacks against the nearest creature that is not you or your allies, or else use its turn to move toward the nearest such target. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on itself on a success."],
"Intaglio": ["Copy one page of non-magical text or art per Magic action onto a medium you supply. Halves spellbook copy time and cost. Concentration, 1 hour.",
 "Touch a surface for the duration. As a Magic action, trace your hand over non-magical text or an image on a surface within range and copy it onto a new medium you provide, such as a book or parchment. Each Magic action copies one page. When you copy a spellbook this way, use the normal rules for replacing a spellbook, but both the time and the GP cost are halved."],
"Investiture of Venom": ["10 minutes: Poison immunity, see who resists Poison, strip a creature's Poison defenses, or blast a 15-ft Line for 4d6 Poison. Concentration.",
 "Your veins swell green and your eyes weep poison. For the duration you gain these benefits. **Immunity.** You have Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition. **Sense.** You can tell which creatures you see within 30 ft have Resistance or Immunity to Poison damage or Immunity to the Poisoned condition. **Strip.** As a Bonus Action, pick a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC. On a fail it loses Resistance to Poison damage, Immunity to Poison damage, or Immunity to the Poisoned condition (your choice of which one it has) until the end of your next turn. **Venom Blast.** As a Magic action, venom blasts from you in a Line 15 ft long and 5 ft wide. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 4d6 Poison damage and is Poisoned until the end of your next turn. On a success it takes half damage only."],
"Life Tether": ["Wisdom save: a tether makes the target take half of any damage you take, as Necrotic. Concentration, 1 minute. More tethers at higher slots.",
 "Choose a creature you see within 120 ft. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail a sickly green tether links you and it. Whenever you take damage, the tethered target takes half as much (round down) as Necrotic damage. If the target drops to 0 HP before the spell ends, you can use a Bonus Action to move the tether to a new creature you see within range. The new target must succeed on a Wisdom save or be tethered. Using a higher slot: you can make more tethers at slot level 4 (two tethers), 6 (three tethers) or 8 (four tethers)."],
"Lifesink": ["15-ft Emanation: others that enter or start there take 4d6 Necrotic, and you regain 4d6 HP plus 1 per creature in it each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "An aura spreads from you in a 15-ft Emanation for the duration. Any other creature that enters the area or starts its turn there takes 4d6 Necrotic damage. At the start of your turn you regain 4d6 HP plus 1 for each creature in the area."],
"Little Death": ["You die and rise as a Ghost for 1d8 hours (rolled secretly by the GM), then return to life with half your HP maximum if your token is on your corpse. Up to 8 hours.",
 "Casting this spell drops you to 0 HP and you die. At the start of your next turn you become a Ghost in the same space as your corpse. Your statistics are replaced by the Ghost stat block, but you keep your HP, Hit Point Dice, Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma scores, and languages. As a Ghost you can only use the abilities in the Ghost stat block, and you add your Proficiency Bonus to its attack rolls and ability DCs. The GM secretly rolls 1d8 when you cast the spell. When that many hours have passed, the spell ends. It ends early if you are reduced to 0 HP as a Ghost or take the Magic action to end it. **Return.** If the Material component (an item of personal sentimental value worth 1+ SP) is still on your corpse when the spell ends, you return to life with HP equal to half your HP maximum. If it is no longer there, you die. **Ruined body.** If your body is destroyed or damaged beyond survival while the spell is active, the duration becomes permanent. You stay a Ghost until your body is targeted by an effect that returns the dead to life such as Raise Dead or Resurrection."],
"Maelfa's Quickened Class": ["10-minute lecture: 10 willing creatures within 30 ft gain a spell, a skill proficiency, or a language you know for 24 hours.",
 "Give a short lecture on a topic of your choice to 10 willing creatures within 30 ft. Choose one spell you know or have prepared, one skill you are proficient in, or one language you can speak, read and write. Each target is temporarily given part of your knowledge. **Spell.** Each target prepares the spell, it counts as on their spell list, and it does not count against their prepared spells. **Skill.** Each target gains proficiency in it. **Language.** Each target can speak, read and write it. The knowledge is lost when the spell ends. If a creature is targeted again while still under an earlier casting, the earlier casting ends. Using a higher slot: duration rises to 30 days at slot level 3 or 4, 10 days at 5 or 6, 30 days at 7 or 8, and 1 year at 9."],
"Magic Mirror": ["Reaction: redirect a spell that targets you to a creature you see within 60 ft. Level 6+ spells need an ability check.",
 "A bubble of iridescent energy flickers between you and a foe. The triggering spell is redirected to a creature of your choice that you see within 60 ft. If the spell is level 5 or lower, you stop being a target and the chosen creature is the target instead. If the spell is level 6 or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the spell's level. On a success you stop being a target and the chosen creature is instead. On a failure you remain the target."],
"Melting Curse": ["Dexterity save: 5d8 Fire and a held or worn metal object melts. Touching the puddle again costs another 5d8 Fire. 1 minute.",
 "Target a creature you see within 100 ft and a metal object it holds or wears. The creature makes a Dexterity save, with Advantage if the object is magical. On a fail it takes 5d8 Fire damage and the object melts and oozes to the ground, where it returns to its normal shape and temperature. If the creature tries to pick up or touch the object for the duration, the object heats and melts again and the creature takes 5d8 Fire damage. The object returns to normal once the creature is no longer touching it or the spell ends. Using a higher slot: +1d8 for each slot level above 6."],
"Mirror Spell": ["Reaction: copy and cast a spell of level 3 or lower that you see someone cast, without a slot or components. Level 3+ needs a check.",
 "Try to copy and cast a spell of level 3 or lower that you see being cast within 60 ft. You can only copy spells cast by creatures and cannot copy your own. If the triggering spell is level 2 or lower you copy and cast it automatically. If it is level 3 or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the triggering spell's level, and you copy it only on a success. The copied spell costs no slot and needs no components. Treat yourself as its original caster, using your own spellcasting ability modifier and spell save DC, and cast it at the lowest level it can be cast. Using a higher slot: the level of the slot you use is the maximum spell level you can copy and cast."],
"Mortality": ["Spend five Hit Point Dice. Charisma save or a planar creature loses that many HP (and HP maximum) and becomes a mortal Humanoid. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "As part of casting you must expend five Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Roll the dice you spent, then choose an Aberration, Celestial, Elemental, Fey or Fiend within 120 ft and condemn it to a taste of mortality. It makes a Charisma save. On a fail its HP maximum and current HP are both reduced by the total you rolled. For the duration, a creature that failed loses all damage Immunities and Resistances, its creature type becomes Humanoid, and it takes an extra 1d4 Necrotic damage each time it takes damage. If an affected creature is reduced to 0 HP, the changes become permanent and the creature dies. That final effect can only be undone by restoring the creature to life and then targeting it with Remove Curse or similar magic. The Material component is a humanoid skull encrusted with gems worth 200+ GP."],
"Neutralize Aura": ["A willing creature cannot be perceived by Fey, Fiends, Celestials and Undead for 1 hour. Ends if it attacks, deals damage, casts, or gets within 5 ft of them. Concentration.",
 "Touch a willing creature and neutralize its aura. Until the spell ends, Fey, Fiends, Celestials and Undead cannot perceive the target. The spell ends early the moment the target makes an attack roll, deals damage, casts a spell, or moves within 5 ft of a creature of one of those types. Using a higher slot: one additional target for each slot level above 1. Casting time is 1 minute."],
"Overgrow": ["Vines pin a creature (Strength save or Restrained) or fix an object in place. Huge or smaller, 60 ft. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Choose a creature or an unworn, uncarried object that is Huge or smaller within 60 ft. Vines grow around it. **Creature.** It makes a Strength save or is Restrained until the spell ends. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. **Object.** It cannot be moved from its spot, and creatures climbing it spend no extra movement. A creature can make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to wrest the object out of the vines so it can be moved. If the object is too heavy for it to move, the attempt fails. Using a higher slot: one additional target for each slot level above 2."],
"Perfection": ["Remake a creature in an Arch Seraph's image: cure Poisoned, suppress curses, full HP, low ability scores become 18, plus one of six blessings. 1 minute.",
 "Speak a holy word and remake a creature you see within 60 ft in the image of the Arch Seraphs. The Poisoned condition ends on it, curses on it are suppressed for the duration, and it is restored to its HP maximum. Each of its ability scores below 18 becomes 18. Depending on the word you use, you also grant a blessing from one Arch Seraph. **Aphaelon.** Immunity to the Charmed condition. When it fails a saving throw it can use a Reaction to reroll and must use the new roll. **Empyreus.** Immunity to the Frightened condition, and it deals an extra 4d6 Force damage to the first target it hits on each of its turns. **Miklas.** Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition, and it regains 4d6 HP at the start of each of its turns. **Morael.** It gains 30 Temporary HP. When an ally within 60 ft of it takes damage, it can use a Reaction to take that damage instead. **Solyma.** Immunity to Thunder damage. When it takes damage from a creature it sees, it can use a Reaction to deal Fire damage to that creature equal to the triggering damage. **Zabriel.** Truesight with a range of 60 ft. At the end of each of its turns it can give Heroic Inspiration to an ally who does not have it."],
"Phoenix Flames": ["You burn up and die in a 30-ft Emanation of holy fire. Constitution save: 30d6 Radiant and 1 Exhaustion, half on a save. You rise after 10 minutes.",
 "You immolate yourself in a cloud of holy flames. You drop to 0 HP and die, and burning radiance erupts from you in a 30-ft Emanation. Each creature in the area makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 30d6 Radiant damage and gains 1 Exhaustion level. On a success it takes half damage only. A creature reduced to 0 HP by this damage is incinerated along with everything nonmagical it wears and carries, and it can be revived only by True Resurrection or Wish. After 10 minutes you rise from the ashes where you cast the spell, returning to life as if targeted by True Resurrection."],
"Power Word Maim": ["Target with 125 HP or fewer takes 8d10 Necrotic and is Prone. Otherwise its Speed is 0 until it saves (Constitution) at a turn end.",
 "Command a creature you see within 60 ft to twist and warp. If it has 125 HP or fewer, it takes 8d10 Necrotic damage and is Prone. If it has more, its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. The target makes a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns, ending the condition on a success."],
"Preserve": ["Food and perishables up to 5 lb in a sack do not age or decay for 12 hours.",
 "Place food and other perishable items weighing 5 lb or less in a sack (holding a pinch of salt) that you touch. For 12 hours they do not age or decay."],
"Primordial Power": ["A touched creature speaks Primordial and gains an elemental boon of your choice (Air, Coldfire, Earth, Fire or Water). Concentration, 1 hour.",
 "Grant a creature you touch a share of elemental power. For the duration it can speak and understand Primordial and gains the benefits of the element you choose. **Air.** Resistance to Lightning and Thunder damage and a Fly Speed of 30 ft. **Coldfire.** Resistance to Cold damage. As a Bonus Action it can expend a Hit Point Die to regain HP equal to the roll plus its Constitution modifier. When it takes Fire damage, it cannot use this Bonus Action on its next turn. **Earth.** Advantage on saves against being moved or knocked Prone, and Tremorsense with a range of 30 ft. **Fire.** Resistance to Fire damage. When a creature within 5 ft of it damages it, it can use a Reaction to make one melee attack against that creature with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike. **Water.** Resistance to Acid damage, the ability to breathe underwater, and a Swim Speed of 60 ft."],
"Reanimate": ["Spend three Hit Point Dice to revive a creature dead for under 10 minutes with 1 HP and temporary HP, a +2 bonus to D20 Tests, then Exhaustion.",
 "As part of casting you must expend three Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Touch a creature that died within the last 10 minutes and return it to life with 1 HP. Roll the dice you spent and the creature gains Temporary HP equal to the roll. At the start of each of its turns it loses 1 of those Temporary HP. While it has Temporary HP from this spell it moves with unnatural vigor and gets a +2 bonus to D20 Tests. When those Temporary HP are gone, it gains 1 Exhaustion level. The spell cannot revive a creature that died of old age and does not restore missing body parts. The Material component is a mix of wilted daisies and herbal powders worth 300+ GP, which the spell consumes."],
"Red Rain": ["Spend eight Hit Point Dice. Blood rain over 5 miles frightens Beasts and Plants and drains exposed creatures with Exhaustion and 2d10 Necrotic per 10 minutes. 8 hours, Concentration.",
 "As part of casting you must expend eight Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Over 1d6 times 5 minutes the sky darkens and thick blood rains everywhere within 5 miles of you. Each Beast and Plant in the area must succeed on a Wisdom save or be Frightened until it has spent 1 minute outside the area. Mundane plants exposed to the rain wither and die after 10 minutes. For every 10 minutes a creature of any type is directly exposed, it gains 1 Exhaustion level and takes 2d10 Necrotic damage, and its HP maximum drops by the Necrotic damage dealt. That reduction lasts until it removes all Exhaustion levels gained from this spell. While it has any such level, it automatically fails saves to end the Poisoned condition. When the spell ends, roll the Hit Point Dice you spent. Beasts and Plants do not return and plants do not regrow in the area for a number of days equal to the total."],
"Ride the Lightning": ["Become lightning along a 5-ft-wide Line up to 60 ft and reappear at the far end. Dexterity save: 4d6 Lightning, half on a save.",
 "Turn yourself into a bolt of lightning and create a 5-ft-wide Line between your space and an unoccupied space within 60 ft. Each creature in the Line makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d6 Lightning damage on a fail or half as much on a success. You then reappear in the chosen space. Using a higher slot: +1d6 damage and +10 ft maximum Line length for each slot level above 4."],
"Sanguine Fusillade": ["Spend seven Hit Point Dice. Target takes Piercing damage equal to the roll, then seven darts burst out. Each dart is a ranged spell attack within 60 ft.",
 "Crystallize a foe's blood into razor darts. As part of casting you must expend seven Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Roll the dice you spent. A creature you see within 60 ft takes Piercing damage equal to the total. When it takes this damage, seven crimson darts burst from it. You can direct each dart at a creature within 60 ft of the original target, one or several, including the original. The darts strike at once. Make a ranged spell attack for each dart. On a hit, roll one of the Hit Point Dice you spent, and the creature takes Piercing damage equal to the number rolled. Using a higher slot: expend one extra Hit Point Die and create one extra dart for each slot level above 7."],
"Sanguine Poppet": ["1 minute cast, spend three Hit Point Dice. A poppet you control (AC 10 + Prof + casting mod, 30 HP) that you can see through and detonate. Concentration, 1 hour.",
 "As part of casting you must expend three Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Smear the Material component (an object shaped like a creature worth 1+ CP) with your blood. It becomes a poppet under your control. Its AC equals 10 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your spellcasting ability modifier, and it has 30 HP. The spell ends if the poppet drops to 0 HP or is more than 1 mile from you. As a Bonus Action you can command it to move 30 ft, and you see and hear through it until the start of your next turn. As a Magic action you can make it burst in a blood explosion, which ends the spell. Roll the dice you spent. Each creature in a 30-ft-radius Sphere centered on the poppet makes a Dexterity save, taking Necrotic damage equal to the roll on a fail or half as much on a success. Using a higher slot: expend one extra Hit Point Die and gain +1 hour of duration for each slot level above 3."],
"Sanguine Shield": ["Spend two Hit Point Dice. Gain 5 Temporary HP per wounded creature within 30 ft (max 15) and Cover while you have them. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "As part of casting you must expend two Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Draw lifeforce from the injured around you into a swirling blood shield. You gain 5 Temporary HP for each creature within 30 ft that is below its HP maximum (including you), up to 15. While you have Temporary HP from this spell, you have Cover. When the spell ends, all Temporary HP from it are lost. Using a higher slot: the maximum rises by 5 for each two slot levels above 2."],
"Seal Spellcasting": ["Charisma save when the target casts: on a fail the slot is spent and the spell does nothing, on a success it takes 3d8 Force. Ends after the save. Concentration, 10 minutes.",
 "Choose a creature you see within 60 ft. When the target next casts a spell, it must make a Charisma save. On a fail it spends the spell slot and casts as normal, but the spell has no effect. On a success it casts the spell and takes 3d8 Force damage. The spell ends immediately after the creature makes this save. Using a higher slot: +1d8 damage for each slot level above 2."],
"Sense Lifeblood": ["Bonus Action, spend two Hit Point Dice. Sense blood kin and the health state of creatures you see, and add Necrotic damage to hits on Bloodied foes. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "As part of casting you must expend two Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. The lifeblood in creatures tells you its secrets. Creatures with Immunity to the Exhaustion condition are immune to this spell. Until the spell ends you can tell whether creatures you see are biologically related. You also know whether a creature's HP is at maximum, below maximum, at half, or below half. Once on each of your turns when you hit a Bloodied creature with an attack roll using a weapon, an Unarmed Strike or a spell, the target takes extra Necrotic damage equal to a roll of one of the Hit Point Dice you spent. Using a higher slot: Concentration can last up to 1 hour at slot level 3 or 4, and up to 8 hours at 5 or higher."],
"Serpent Tongue": ["Bonus Action melee spell attack within 10 ft: 1d12 Piercing and Poisoned for the duration. 1 minute.",
 "Turn your tongue into a venomous serpent for the duration. As a Bonus Action, make a melee spell attack against a creature within 10 ft. On a hit it takes 1d12 Piercing damage and is Poisoned for the rest of the spell. Using a higher slot: +1d12 damage for each slot level above 3."],
"Shared Judgement": ["Once per turn when you drop an Undead to 0 HP, deal 5d6 Radiant to a creature you see within 60 ft. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Once on each of your turns when you reduce an Undead to 0 HP, you can deal 5d6 Radiant damage to a creature you see within 60 ft of you, with no action required. Using a higher slot: +1d6 damage for each slot level above 4."],
"Shroud Blood": ["Spend one Hit Point Die. A creature gets Advantage on Stealth checks and can regain Invisibility as a Reaction for rounds equal to dice spent. Concentration, 10 minutes.",
 "As part of casting you must expend one Hit Point Die or the spell fails. Choose yourself or a willing creature within 30 ft. The target has Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. When the target loses the Invisible condition, it can use a Reaction to become Invisible again for a number of rounds equal to the Hit Point Dice you spent. It loses the Invisible condition right after it makes an attack roll, deals damage or casts a spell. Using a higher slot: one additional target for each slot level above 1."],
"Somnolence": ["Spend one Hit Point Die. Roll it plus 2d12. If the total meets a creature's current HP it sleeps 1 minute, or 24 hours if it meets its HP maximum.",
 "As part of casting you must expend one Hit Point Die or the spell fails. Roll the die you spent plus 2d12 and choose a creature within 30 ft. If the total is equal to or greater than its current HP, it falls into a magical slumber for 1 minute. If the total is equal to or greater than its HP maximum, the slumber lasts 24 hours. The spell ends on a target if it takes damage or someone within 5 ft takes an action to shake it awake. A creature woken early gains 1 Exhaustion level. Creatures that do not sleep, such as elves, and creatures with Immunity to the Exhaustion condition automatically succeed on saves against this spell. **The Long Sleep.** The Prismatic Circle uses a variant that takes 10 minutes and a Humanoid sacrifice. Its adherents believe the ritual holds back the waking of Gormadraug for a day and a night. Using a higher slot: roll an extra 1d12 and expend two additional Hit Point Dice for each slot level above 1."],
"Spirit Swarm": ["Charisma save: 8d8 Psychic and Frightened (half damage on a save). The target needs Charisma 3 or higher. 120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Invite spirits to take revenge on a creature you see within 120 ft. The target must have a Charisma of 3 or higher. It makes a Charisma save. On a fail it takes 8d8 Psychic damage and is Frightened until the spell ends. On a success it takes half damage only."],
"Splattering Smite": ["Reaction, spend five Hit Point Dice. Once per turn when you hit with a Melee weapon or Unarmed Strike, regain HP equal to a roll of one die spent. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Your strikes drink the blood of your foes. As part of casting you must expend five Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with an attack roll using a Melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike, roll one of the Hit Point Dice you spent and regain HP equal to the number rolled."],
"Steal Immortality": ["Reaction, spend nine Hit Point Dice. Gain twice the roll as Temporary HP and take the target's creature type and its benefits, plus Poison immunity and physical Resistance.",
 "As part of casting you must expend nine Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Roll the dice you spent and gain Temporary HP equal to twice the total. You gain the creature type of the spell's target in addition to your own. While the spell lasts you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition, you no longer need to eat, drink or breathe, and you have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. You also gain a benefit based on the new type. **Celestial.** Resistance to Radiant and Necrotic damage and a Fly Speed of 60 ft. **Elemental.** Resistance to Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning and Thunder damage. **Fey.** As a Bonus Action, become Invisible until the start of your next turn, or teleport up to 60 ft to an unoccupied space you see. **Fiend.** Resistance to Cold and Fire damage and a Fly Speed of 60 ft. **Undead.** Immunity to Necrotic damage and to the Charmed and Frightened conditions. You keep the creature type and benefits until you cast the spell again or drop to 0 HP. Range 300 ft. The Material component is a gem-encrusted humanoid skull worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes."],
"Suffocate": ["Ranged spell attack: force hands Restrain a creature within 60 ft, which cannot breathe and gains Exhaustion once out of breath. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Create a pair of grasping hands of invisible force and make a ranged spell attack against a creature you see within 60 ft. On a hit it is Restrained, and while Restrained it cannot breathe. A creature can hold its breath for rounds equal to 1 plus its Constitution modifier (minimum 30 seconds) before suffocation begins. When it runs out of breath, it gains 1 Exhaustion level at the end of each of its turns. When it can breathe again, it removes all Exhaustion levels gained from suffocating. A creature Restrained by the hands can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC and is freed on a success."],
"Summon Plant": ["Call a Plant Spirit ally with a Blooming, Oaken or Thorny feature. It acts right after you and lasts up to 1 hour. Concentration.",
 "Call forth a plant spirit in an unoccupied space you see within 90 ft. It uses the Plant Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a floral feature: Blooming, Oaken or Thorny. The feature determines one of the traits in the stat block. The creature disappears at 0 HP or when the spell ends. It is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its move to avoid danger. The Material component is a ceramic pot of herbs and fertilizer worth at least 200 GP. Using a higher slot: use the slot's level as the spell level in the stat block."],
"Summon Sea Spirit": ["Call a Sea Serpent Spirit ally with an Enormous Mouth, Glowing Lantern or Scaled Wings feature. It acts right after you and lasts up to 1 hour. Concentration.",
 "Call forth an abyssal spirit in an unoccupied space you see within 90 ft. It uses the Sea Serpent Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose an abhorrent feature: Enormous Mouth, Glowing Lantern or Scaled Wings. The feature determines one of the traits in the stat block. The creature disappears at 0 HP or when the spell ends. It is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn right after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its move to avoid danger. The Material component is a bejeweled sea serpent statuette worth at least 300 GP. Using a higher slot: use the slot's level as the spell level in the stat block."],
"Supernal Smite": ["Bonus Action on a hit: extra 4d6 Force, breaks Concentration, and ends ongoing spells of level 3 or lower on the target (checks for level 4+).",
 "A strike makes the ambient magic around a creature collapse and detonate. The target you hit takes an extra 4d6 Force damage from the attack. If it is concentrating on a spell, that Concentration is broken. Each ongoing spell of level 3 or lower on the target ends. For each ongoing spell of level 4 or higher on it, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus that spell's level. On a success the spell ends."],
"Theft of Vitae": ["Reaction: the triggering creature takes Necrotic damage equal to a Hit Point Die roll, and you gain Temporary HP equal to that plus the triggering damage (max 15).",
 "Roll one of the Hit Point Dice you expended to cast the spell. The triggering creature takes Necrotic damage equal to the result. You gain Temporary HP equal to the result plus the triggering damage, to a maximum of 15. Using a higher slot: the maximum rises by 10 for each slot level above 2."],
"Thorn Armor": ["A willing creature gains 3d6 Temporary HP. Melee attackers take Piercing damage equal to the Temporary HP they remove. 10 minutes.",
 "A flexible, thorny exoskeleton appears around a willing target you touch. It gains 3d6 Temporary HP. If a creature hits the target with a melee attack roll before the spell ends, that creature takes Piercing damage equal to the number of Temporary HP lost from the attack. The spell ends early if the target has no Temporary HP left from it. Using a higher slot: +2d6 Temporary HP for each slot level above 1."],
"Tremor": ["15-ft Emanation of shaking ground: Difficult Terrain, Dexterity save or 1d6 Bludgeoning and Prone, once per turn per creature. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "The ground in a 15-ft Emanation around you shakes violently. You are unaffected. The area is Difficult Terrain. Whenever the Emanation enters a creature's space, a creature enters the Emanation, or a creature ends its turn there, it makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 1d6 Bludgeoning damage and is Prone. A creature makes this save only once per turn. Using a higher slot: +1d6 damage for each slot level above 1."],
"Undead Enthrallment": ["1 hour cast. Raise corpses as Undead of CR 3 or lower under your command for 24 hours. Recast to keep control. Up to four controlled.",
 "Choose a corpse or several within 10 ft that together match the size of the creature you are animating (the GM decides how many corpses are needed). The spell raises them as Undead creatures of CR 3 or lower, and the GM has their statistics. On each of your turns you can use a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature made by this spell that is within 60 ft of you. You can command any or all of them at once with the same command. You decide its action and movement for its next turn, or give a general order such as guarding a room or corridor. With no command it takes the Dodge action. It keeps following an order until the task is done. The creature obeys you for 24 hours. To keep control for another 24 hours, recast the spell on it before the period ends. That casting renews control of 1 creature already animated by this spell instead of animating a new one. A creature you have kept for 30 days stays under your control permanently. You can control at most four creatures with this spell. The Material components are a clay pot of brackish water, a clay pot of grave dirt, and a black onyx stone worth 500+ GP for each corpse."],
"Vampiric Claws": ["Bonus Action: claws make your Unarmed Strike deal 1d6 Slashing using your spellcasting modifier, and each hit grants Temporary HP equal to that modifier. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "You sprout wicked claws. When your Unarmed Strike deals damage with them, it deals 1d6 Slashing damage instead of its normal damage, and you use your spellcasting ability modifier for the attack and damage rolls instead of Strength. While the spell lasts, each time you deal damage with an Unarmed Strike, you gain Temporary HP equal to your spellcasting ability modifier. Those Temporary HP are lost when the spell ends."],
"Vibrating Humors": ["Spend one Hit Point Die. Constitution save or Thunder damage equal to the roll and Disadvantage on Stealth, repeating each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "As part of casting you must expend one Hit Point Die or the spell fails. A creature you see within 30 ft makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes Thunder damage equal to a roll of the die you spent and has Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks because its blood hums loudly. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success. Using a higher slot: expend one additional Hit Point Die for each slot level above 1 to increase the damage."],
"Viscous Sheath": ["Spend seven Hit Point Dice. Melee attackers take Necrotic damage equal to a die roll plus your casting modifier, and you can trap their weapons. 10 minutes.",
 "As part of casting you must expend seven Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. Clotted blood wraps your body. Whenever a creature within 5 ft hits you with a melee attack roll, it takes Necrotic damage equal to a roll of one of the dice you spent plus your spellcasting ability modifier. When a creature hits you with a Melee weapon, you can use a Reaction to make clots form around the weapon. The attacker must succeed on a Strength save or the weapon sticks to you. While the weapon is stuck, it cannot be used, and the attacker is Grappled unless it releases the weapon. The attacker can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to free the weapon, or release the weapon to end the Grappled condition. You can trap a number of weapons equal to the Hit Point Dice you spent. When the spell ends the weapons are released. The Material component is a bloody funerary shroud. Using a higher slot: trap one additional weapon for each slot level above 4."],
"Wall of Gloom": ["Wall of grief-energy up to 60 ft long or a 20-ft-diameter ring, blocks sight, Charisma saves for Incapacitated nearby and Exhaustion inside. 10 minutes.",
 "Create a wall of swirling gray energy made of the psychic pain of loss, on a solid surface within 120 ft. Make it up to 60 ft long, 10 ft high and 5 ft thick, or a ring with a 20-ft diameter, up to 20 ft high and 5 ft thick. The wall blocks line of sight and sheds Dim Light out to 100 ft. When you cast it, you and creatures you designate can pass through and stay near it unharmed. Any other creature that moves within 20 ft of it or starts its turn there must succeed on a Charisma save or be Incapacitated until the start of its next turn. A creature can move through the wall, but it is emotionally draining. The first time a creature enters the wall on a turn or ends its turn in it, it must succeed on a Charisma save or gain 1 Exhaustion level."],
"Weave Numen": ["Sense magic within 120 ft and gain 13 threads to boost your spells, interrupt enemy spells, or add 4 damage or healing per thread. Concentration, 10 minutes.",
 "You sense magic within 120 ft. You see a faint aura around any visible creature or object there that bears magic and learn its school of magic, if any. You also gain thirteen threads. Spend them as follows. **Enhance.** When you cast a spell, spend 1 thread (no action) to enhance it as if you had used a slot 1 level higher, and gain Temporary HP equal to 1 plus the spell's level. **Interrupt.** When a creature you see within 120 ft casts a spell, spend 1 thread as a Reaction to interrupt it. A spell of level 3 or lower fails with no effect. For a spell of level 4 or higher, make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 plus the spell's level, and on a success the spell fails with no effect. **Amplify.** When you cast a spell that heals or damages a creature, spend up to six threads (no action). The healing or damage to one creature increases by four times the threads spent. You lose any remaining threads when the spell ends, and the spell ends if you spend them all. The Material component is a mithral sewing needle worth 300+ GP, which the spell consumes. Using a higher slot: gain two more threads for each slot level above 6."],
"Wilting Smite": ["Bonus Action, spend two Hit Point Dice. The creature you hit loses all damage Resistances until your next turn and takes extra Necrotic damage.",
 "As part of casting you must expend two Hit Point Dice or the spell fails. The creature you hit with the strike loses all Resistances to damage until the start of your next turn and takes extra Necrotic damage from the attack. Roll one of the Hit Point Dice you spent to determine the damage."],
"Wipe Face": ["Curse a creature within 60 ft: its face smooths over, leaving it Blinded, Incapacitated and suffocating. Constitution save each turn to end it. Concentration, 10 minutes.",
 "Curse a creature you see within 60 ft. Its face is replaced by smooth skin that seals its eyes, nose and mouth. It is Blinded and Incapacitated and begins suffocating. At the end of each of its turns it can make a Constitution save to end the spell. Dealing at least 15 Slashing damage to it opens an airway so it can breathe, but the curse seals the opening again at the start of your next turn."],
"Wrack": ["Constitution save or the target's Speed is halved and it has Disadvantage on attack rolls. Repeat the save each turn. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "Choose a creature you see within 30 ft. It must succeed on a Constitution save or suffer painful muscle spasms for the duration. On a fail its Speed is halved and it has Disadvantage on attack rolls. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success."],
}
